  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati-Australia Uaroko Program (KiriUP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kiribati-Australia Uaroko Program (KiriUP) is the Australian Government&apos;s bilateral GEDSI programme in Kiribati. Its goal is: Women, girls and people living with disabilities in Kiribati, in all their diversity, are safe and empowered to equitably share in resources, opportunities and decision making. The programme has a major focus on gender equality and disability and social inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
